    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required exposing `checkDigit` on the owner \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. The test (`AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`) recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts it equals the returned `checkDigit`.\n\nTwo edits, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient public Integer getCheckDigit()` that delegates to the already-present `luhnCheckDigit(...)` helper, computing the digit over `customerCode`. The existing Luhn implementation matches the test's algorithm exactly (right-to-left, doubling every second digit).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema. This generates the field on `OwnerDto`, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name from `Owner.getCheckDigit()` \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
